    "html": "<p>The relationship between the period of a planet’s orbit <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span> and the distance to the Sun <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> can be expressed as <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T^{n}∝R^{m}\"></span> where n and m are constants.</p>\n<p>What is a possible pair of values for n and m?<br/><br/></p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>[1]</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Option A is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"B\">Option B is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"C\">Option C is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"D\">Option D is shown in the figure above.</li></ol>"
